1. Create a consistent battle glass treatment

Introduce or consolidate reusable CSS variables/classes for a lightweight semi-transparent dark glass appearance suitable for overlays on top of animated stage artwork.

The glass should feel consistent with Alva’s existing Home glass treatment, but it must remain highly readable over bright and dark portions of the stages.

The treatment should generally include:

* semi-transparent near-black/charcoal background rather than an opaque var(--surface)
* subtle translucent white edge/border
* restrained highlight or gradient to give it a glass-like surface
* readable white/off-white text
* appropriate shadow where needed
* optional subtle backdrop-filter / blur only if it performs well
* a graceful fallback if backdrop filtering is unavailable

Do not make the glass excessively bright, frosted, milky, or glossy. It should still look like Alva.

Be careful with mobile performance: this is a 60 FPS Canvas fighting game. Prefer a restrained effect over an expensive large-area blur.

